From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:57:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: passkey and security-key dialog drawn by
 the shell

Plan C21. Chrome's WebAuthn dialog is a tab-modal Views sheet of a Browser
window; without one, navigator.credentials.create()/get() showed nothing
and timed out. With the //chrome hooks of the earlier patch:

- The bridge's AuthenticatorRequestDialogViewController describes the
  request flow's current step as an OACWebAuthnDialog (OACWebAuthn.h): the
  method list (passkeys on this Mac, this Mac, security key), confirmation,
  "touch your security key", PIN entry / setup / change with Chromium's
  error and attempts, touch again, fingerprint enrollment, account choice,
  passkey creation, the private-window notice and errors with "try again".
  Each change comes as -tab:didUpdateWebAuthnDialog:. The shell's choices
  become the model's events, as Chrome's sheets send them; cancel (the
  default) ends the request with NotAllowedError. The model closing its
  view (done, or macOS's Touch ID / password prompt took over) withdraws
  the request.
- Passkeys on this Mac use the keychain access group
  <team id>.<bundle id>.webauthn of the running app's signature
  (SecCodeCopySigningInformation) instead of Chrome's compile-time group.
  An ad-hoc build has no team: passkeys on this Mac are then unavailable
  (device/fido checks the keychain-access-groups entitlement) and security
  keys still work.
- Not offered: iCloud Keychain passkeys (Apple's restricted
  com.apple.developer.web-browser.public-key-credential entitlement), phones
  (hybrid: Bluetooth and the QR flow) and Google Password Manager; such a
  step shows an "unsupported" error the user can back out of.
